  1944  (1284)  % ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1945  (1285)  % STILL NOT DONE, and worth saying rather than leaving to be met:
  1946  (1286)  %
  1947  (1287)  %  1. THIS ITEM USED TO READ "Nothing has been compiled", and it is kept here
  1948  (1288)  %     in corrected form rather than deleted, because everything it worried about
  1949  (1289)  %     has now been settled by the compiler itself rather than by argument:
  1950  (1290)  %     INTEGER4, two-dimensional BYTES ARRAY, the implicit extra ARRAY keyword on
  1951  (1291)  %     a BYTES declaration, BOOLEAN := TRUE, and the XMMSGIDENTIFIER and
  1952  (1292)  %     XMUSERADDRESS names out of XMP-B02:IMPT. All of it compiles and runs.
  1953  (1293)  %
  1954  (1294)  %     The one thing the list did NOT anticipate is the one that cost the most:
  1955  (1295)  %     a letter arrives with its XSLET header still in front of it. No amount of
  1956  (1296)  %     checking declarations against a manual would have found that - only the
  1957  (1297)  %     raw dump did.
  1958  (1298)  %
  1959  (1299)  %  2. The seat returned on Leave uses XMPINFC(flags, portNumber, extraConn,
  1960  (1300)  %     serialNumber). Its reply comes back later on our own port as an ordinary
  1961  (1301)  %     message, which handleMessage will see and not understand. Decide what to
  1962  (1302)  %     do with it - ignoring an unknown kind is already the behaviour, so this
  1963  (1303)  %     is safe, but it is safe by accident until somebody says so.
  1964  (1304)  %
  1965  (1305)  %  3. Each reason string carries its length as a separate constant, because
  1966  (1306)  %     PLANC has no LENGTH routine and SIZE's meaning for a BYTES parameter is
  1967  (1307)  %     not established. A string and its number must be changed together.
  1968  (1308)  % ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
